{
  "text": "On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said, The Messenger of Allah, may the blessings and peace of Allah be upon him, said, Do not vary one another. Do not inflate prices one to another. Do not hate one another. Do not turn away from one another. And do not undercut one another. But be you, O servants of Allah, brother. But be you, O servants of Allah, brothers. A Muslim is the brother of a Muslim. He neither oppresses nor does he fail him. He neither lies to him nor does he hold him in contempt. Piety is right here. And he pointed to his breast three times. It is evil enough for a man to hold his brother Muslim in contempt. The whole of a Muslim for another Muslim is inviolable. His blood, his property and his honour. It was related by Muslim.",
